    "narrative": "With today's slate heavily impacted by team off-days for core assets like **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood**, the offensive burden falls squarely on **Brice Turang**. Facing the elite arm of Skubal (2.85 xERA), **Brice Turang** earns a marginal 46.51 score; while his raw hitting projection is suppressed by the matchup, his aggressive base-running upside is optimized by Skubal\u2019s slower delivery, which provides the necessary cushion to keep him in the lineup despite the unfavorable SP profile. With **Tyler Soderstrom** sidelined on the IL, our roster depth is tested, forcing a conservative approach to preserve our remaining game caps for higher-leverage opportunities later in the week.\n\nThe bench decision-making process was straightforward today given the lack of active options, but the proximity of players like **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** to the \"marginal\" threshold remains a point of focus for our daily rotation. **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, and **Isaac Paredes** are currently being preserved to exploit more favorable SP xERA matchups in upcoming series. We are also closely monitoring the development of our prospects, including **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana**, as we look for any situational platoon edges that might justify a spot start. Currently, **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains our primary bench-stashed priority once the schedule softens, as we avoid exposure to today\u2019s high-velocity, low-ceiling pitching environment to protect our season-long WHIP and AVG integrity.",
